---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import { getIndex, getSyndication, getTags } from "../lib/data"

const index = getIndex()
const syndication = getSyndication()
const tags = getTags()
const sourceRows = Object.entries(syndication.method.weights)
const buildCount = index.models.reduce((total, model) => total + model.builds, 0)
---

<Base title="Method" description="How the Democratic AI catalogue defines reciprocity, tags models, scores independent listings, and records evidence.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h1>What counts, and how we check it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Democratic AI is reciprocal AI. Every model learns from the commons. This catalogue records what a release
        gives back, and whether independent registries picked it up.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap detail-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Release terms, not a grade</h2>
        <p>
          The tier records how much of the release is open: weights, training data, recipe, and access. It is not a
          quality score or a moral grade. <strong>Open-weight is a real return to the commons.</strong> Open data and
          open code add to it. The catalogue records the difference without treating open-weight as a failure.
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><span class="badge badge-commons">commons</span></td><td>Weights, training data, and training code are open, with a reusable licence.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="badge badge-reciprocal">reciprocal</span></td><td>Weights and recipe are open, data is open or documented, with a reusable licence.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="badge badge-shared">shared</span></td><td>Weights are available, but the data is closed or the licence restricts reuse.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="badge badge-closed">closed</span></td><td>The weights are not available.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="badge badge-unproven">unproven</span></td><td>The evidence is not sufficient to make a determination.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.88rem;margin-top:0.8rem">
          Most records are <strong>unproven</strong> on training data today. That means the data statement is
          unchecked, not that the model is closed. Open-weight is a real contribution; open data and open code add
          to it. A conditional licence can cap a record at <strong>shared</strong> before the data question is
          resolved. The next pass will assess training data and code.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>The scorecard</h2>
        <p>
          The catalogue carries its own current scorecard. It does not repeat a frozen table from an earlier essay.
          Each axis is independent, and each value is recomputed from the evidence the record holds today.
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Axis</th><th>What it measures</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><strong>Openness/Morality</strong></td><td>What the release gives back: open weights, open training data, open training code, and reuse terms. The score is computed from the record, not assigned by hand.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Performance/Intelligence</strong></td><td>The model's current measured performance on its task. For coding models this is a primary agentic benchmark composite; for speech models it is average WER; for other models it is the best current primary benchmark. The number is an index, not a percentage.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Research/Citation</strong></td><td>Current research benchmarks where they exist. Citation accuracy is a separate question, and the record says when it is not measured.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Syndication</strong></td><td>Independent listings, not quality. The model's own host has weight 0. A build inherits its base model's score.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.88rem;margin-top:0.8rem">
          A model can be strong on openness and weak on citation. A model can be a strong coder and a poor
          citizen. The scorecard keeps those judgements apart. <strong>Missing is not zero.</strong> A score without
          a current source is not shown.
          <a href="/thesis/">Read the argument</a>.
        </p>
        <h3>How the numbers are made</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Openness/Morality</strong> starts from the release terms: 50 for open weights, 25 for open training data, 15 for open training code, and up to 10 for a reuse-permitting licence. Unchecked data and code add nothing; they are not treated as closed.</li>
          <li><strong>Performance/Intelligence</strong> uses the mean of the available primary benchmarks: SWE-bench Verified, SWE-bench Pro, Terminal-Bench 2.x, and LiveCodeBench. A model-card figure fills a gap only when the aggregator has no primary row. A later update may inherit its base model's primary result when it has no comparable benchmark of its own, and the record says so.</li>
          <li><strong>Research/Citation</strong> uses current research benchmarks such as BrowseComp and DeepSearchQA. It does not claim citation accuracy.</li>
          <li><strong>Syndication</strong> counts independent listings. It is 0–10, not an index.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>A build is not a model</h2>
        <p>
          A GGUF, MLX, CoreML, ONNX, FP8, or quantized release is packaging. It inherits the base model's task and
          terms. It does not get its own page.
        </p>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.9rem">
          This index has {index.models.length} root and notable models with {buildCount} attached builds.
          {syndication.counts.builds_and_probes_skipped} builds, probes, and documentation items were skipped as
          records.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>The syndication score</h2>
        <p>
          The score counts independent listings. It is not a quality score, a reciprocity tier, or a measure of
          openness. A closed model can score 10. A reciprocal model can score 0.
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Kind</th><th>Weight</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {sourceRows.map(([id, weight]) => (
                <tr><td>{id}</td><td>{id === "models.dev" || id === "agent-detect" ? "registry" : id === "research" ? "research" : id === "hugging-face" ? "host (self)" : "aggregator or evaluation"}</td><td>{weight}</td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.88rem;margin-top:0.8rem">
          The model's own Hugging Face page has weight 0. A build inherits the base model's score. Every point links
          to the listing.
        </p>
        {syndication.unavailable_sources.map((source) => (
          <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.88rem">
            <strong>{source.id}</strong> is a worthwhile source, but it is not scored yet: {source.reason}
          </p>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Evidence rules</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Never guess. A missing field is <code>unknown</code>.</li>
          <li>The licence file beats the model card. The model card beats a news article.</li>
          <li>Record conflicts. Do not average them.</li>
          <li>Record the date of every check.</li>
          <li>Do not infer from silence. No data statement is not proof of closed data.</li>
          <li>Journal every tier change.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>How the index is built</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>A pull records source-native metadata from Hugging Face, X, GitHub, arXiv, and sitemaps.</li>
          <li>A rules pass assigns source-native and specific title or text tags.</li>
          <li>Clef, a Cloudflare decision model, confirms only the models left in review. It answers yes/no per task, at 0.8 or above.</li>
          <li>Builds and probes are separated from roots. A build attaches to its base.</li>
          <li>Independent listings produce the syndication score.</li>
          <li>One record is written per root or notable model.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.88rem">
          Nothing is trained or hosted here. The repository records evidence and links.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Now</h2>
        <dl class="definition">
          <dt>Root models</dt><dd>{index.models.length}</dd>
          <dt>Builds attached</dt><dd>{buildCount}</dd>
          <dt>Independent listings</dt><dd>{index.models.filter((model) => model.score > 0).length}</dd>
          <dt>Very strong</dt><dd>{index.models.filter((model) => model.band === "very-strong").length}</dd>
          <dt>Average score</dt><dd>{syndication.counts.average_score}/10</dd>
          <dt>Tag namespaces</dt><dd>{Object.keys(tags.namespaces).length}</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Read more</h2>
        <ul class="source-list">
          <li><a href="/data/">The JSON API</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/bevry-vibes/democratic-ai/blob/main/DESIGN.md">DESIGN.md</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/bevry-vibes/democratic-ai/blob/main/.plans/1794621986000-democratic-ai-catalogue.md">The research plan</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/bevry-vibes/agent-detect">agent-detect</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://models.dev">models.dev</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h2>Correct a record</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.9rem">
          Open an issue with a source. A correction with evidence is always welcome.
        </p>
        <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/bevry-vibes/democratic-ai/issues">Open an issue</a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</Base>
